# Which UCLA ROMS namelist vocabulary each roms_gpu release reads.
#
# A release reads the namelist groups and keys of the UCLA ROMS release named
# here, plus its own optional groups below. Groups it does not read are
# ignored; a CPU feature switch it does not have stops the run at start-up
# (src/host/feature_guard.F90). From v0.1.2-beta, a key it does not know in a
# group it reads stops the run at start-up, naming the group (before, the rest
# of that group silently kept its defaults).
#
# Keys added in later UCLA ROMS releases that roms_gpu reads (after
# v0.1.3-beta; before, a namelist with them stopped at the read):
#   0.12.0  &cdr_lite_settings  cdr_carbonate_sensitivity_time_interpolation
#           as UCLA ROMS: .true. (default) interpolates ddic_dco2 and
#           ddic_dalk linearly in time; .false. holds each record until the
#           model time passes the next one (the first step of a run takes
#           the record at or before its time), without the missing-record
#           rule (the CPU applies it only with interpolation).
#   0.13.0  &v_sponge_settings  v_sponge_trc
#           as UCLA ROMS: the maximum tracer diffusivity of the sponge
#           layer (m^2/s); negative or absent: v_sponge; 0: a sponge on the
#           currents only. Every tracer (T, S, the passive, CDR_LITE and
#           MARBL tracers) gets it. v_sponge = 0 with v_sponge_trc > 0
#           gives a sponge on the tracers only. Output files carry the
#           global attributes v_sponge, v_sponge_trc and their _units, as
#           UCLA ROMS.
#   after 0.16.0  &v_sponge_settings  use_boundary_sponge
#           as UCLA ROMS (there it replaces the SPONGE cpp key): .true.
#           (default) adds the sponge along the open boundaries with the
#           maxima v_sponge and v_sponge_trc (no sponge if both are 0);
#           .false. adds none, and the output files do not carry the
#           v_sponge attributes. A negative v_sponge stops the run. UCLA
#           ROMS 0.16.0 and earlier do not read the key: there the SPONGE
#           cpp key decides, and a build without it ignores v_sponge.
#
# GPU-only additions: the optional group &tile_settings (tile balancing),
# &passive_tracers (n_passive, init_mode), and in
# &param_settings the key n. Removed after v0.1.3-beta (unused; a namelist
# that sets them now stops at the read): &param_settings nsub_x, nsub_e and
# ntrc_bio (not UCLA ROMS keys), &bgc_settings nbgc_flx (UCLA ROMS still
# reads it, unused, and its template does not set it). The GPU-only groups
# &flux_frc_settings and &bulk_frc_settings (unused copies of
# &surf_frc_settings keys) are no longer read, so they are ignored.
#
# UCLA ROMS settings that roms_gpu reads but cannot honour stop the run at
# start-up with a message naming the key (after v0.1.3-beta; before, they
# were ignored or, for diag_uv and diag_trc, gave a warning):
#   &ts_output_settings        wrt_temp_dia, wrt_salt_dia = .true.
#   &diagnostics_settings      diag_uv, diag_trc = .true.
#   &surf_flx_output_settings  wrt_swflx = .true.
#   &implicit_fs               fs_selftest > 0 with fs_mode = 'implicit'
#                              (UCLA ROMS runs the self-test only there)
#   &marbl_biogeochemistry_settings
#     marbl_diagnostics_to_write: in a run with wrt_bgc_dia_his or
#     wrt_bgc_dia_avg, the name of a MARBL diagnostic outside the set the
#     GPU computes (PH, pCO2SURF, DpCO2, FG_CO2, FG_ALT_CO2, PH_ALT_CO2,
#     pCO2SURF_ALT_CO2, zsatcalc, zsatarag, CO3, CO3_ALT_CO2,
#     co3_sat_calc, co3_sat_arag). An empty list writes that set (UCLA
#     ROMS: all of MARBL's). do_cdr_output does not need the list.
#     marbl_config_file: a non-empty name of a file that does not exist
#     (before, the GPU ran MARBL with its default settings); "" runs MARBL
#     with its defaults, as UCLA ROMS. The path is relative to the
#     namelist file.
#
# &nhmg_settings nhmg = .true. stops the run at start-up: roms_gpu has no
# non-hydrostatic solver. (UCLA ROMS from its run-time NHMG switch,
# unreleased; before, NHMG was a cpp key the GPU could not see.)
#
# &surf_frc_settings check_bulk_frc_units = .true. (after v0.1.3-beta;
# before, ignored): as UCLA ROMS, with bulk forcing, after the first step's
# fluxes the units attribute of qair must be 'kg/kg' and of rain 'cm/day'
# in the file of the record read last; otherwise the run stops. No effect
# with flux forcing.
#
# Passive tracers in history files: &ts_output_settings wrt_passive (default
# .true.), as UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0, puts the generic passive and CDR_LITE
# tracers in _his. It replaces write_passive in the GPU-only group
# &passive_tracers; a namelist that still has that key stops at the read.
#
# Averages of temperature and salinity: &ts_output_settings wrt_avg_temp
# and wrt_avg_salt (default .false., as UCLA ROMS) put temp and salt in the
# _avg file. As on UCLA ROMS, with MARBL the tracers selected by
# marbl_tracers_to_write are averaged too: an empty list (every tracer) or
# a list naming temp or salt averages them whatever wrt_avg_temp and
# wrt_avg_salt say. Before, the GPU averaged T and S only through that
# list (without MARBL, never), which the default .false. keeps.
#
# MARBL forcing: logical keys in &bgc_settings (default .true.) switch the
# reading of atmospheric xCO2 and nitrogen deposition from the forcing
# files, as in UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0; before, UCLA ROMS selected them with
# cpp keys (PCO2AIR_FORCING, NOX_FORCING, NHY_FORCING) and the GPU read what
# the files held:
#   use_xco2air_forcing   xco2_air and xco2_air_alt; .false.: both are
#                         xco2air_default (ppm, default 284.7)
#   use_nox_forcing       nox; .false.: 0
#   use_nhy_forcing       nhy; .false.: 0
# A variable that is on and in no file stops the run; so do dust and iron,
# which have no switch.
#
# BGC output: &bgc_settings wrt_bgc_his, wrt_bgc_avg, wrt_bgc_dia_his and
# wrt_bgc_dia_avg (default .false.) write _bgc, _bgc_avg, _bgc_dia and
# _bgc_dia_avg with their output_period_bgc_* and nrpf_bgc_* (default 0: the
# run stops if the stream is on), as UCLA ROMS. Before, the MARBL tracers and
# diagnostics were in _his and only wrt_bgc_avg was honoured. Without MARBL
# (use_marbl = .false.) the switches do nothing, as on UCLA ROMS.
#
# Surface forcing: &surf_frc_settings surf_frc_type, as UCLA ROMS after
# 0.16.0 (there it replaces the cpp keys BULK_FRC and ANA_SMFLUX, ANA_STFLUX,
# ANA_SSFLUX, ANA_SRFLUX): 'bulk' (the default), 'flux' or 'none' (no surface
# fluxes). It alone decides; before, the GPU used bulk forcing when the files
# held its variables, flux forcing when they held sustr, svstr and shflux,
# and none otherwise. Every variable of the chosen type must be in the
# forcing files, as on UCLA ROMS (bulk: uwnd, vwnd, Tair, qair, rain, lwrad,
# swrad; flux: sustr, svstr, shflux, swflux, swrad); before, rain, lwrad and
# swrad (bulk) and swflux and swrad (flux) were 0 when missing. A flux-forced
# case must set surf_frc_type = 'flux', and one without surface forcing
# 'none'. The restoring switches need 'bulk'.
#
# File layout: &pio_settings parallel_io (default .true.), as UCLA ROMS after
# 0.16.0 (there it goes with the build option make PIO=yes, which replaces
# the cpp key PARALLEL_IO). .true. means joined files, the only layout the
# GPU reads and writes; .false. (UCLA ROMS's per-rank files, its default
# build) stops the run. The group is read in every run; pio_stride and
# pio_direct_read (UCLA ROMS's PIO tuning) are read and ignored. UCLA ROMS's
# template sets parallel_io = .false., so a namelist made from it must set
# .true. (or drop the key) to run on the GPU.
#
# MARBL on or off: &marbl_biogeochemistry_settings use_marbl (default .false.;
# a missing group is .false.), as UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0 (there it goes with
# the build option make MARBL=yes, which replaces the cpp key MARBL). The
# group is read in every run, and use_marbl alone switches MARBL on; before,
# nt_bgc > 0 did. nt_bgc (&param_settings) must be 0 without use_marbl and
# MARBL's tracer count (32 with the default settings) with it; otherwise the
# run stops. A MARBL case must add use_marbl = .true.
#
# Salinity and MPI masking, as UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0 (there they replace
# the cpp keys SALINITY and MPI_MASKING): &param_settings salinity (default
# .true.) is read, and .false. (a temperature-only run) stops: the GPU always
# carries salinity. &param_settings mpi_masking (default .false.; UCLA ROMS
# drops all-land tiles and chooses its tiling) is read and ignored.
#
# Analytical cases and small switches, as UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0 (there
# they replace the cpp keys ANA_GRID, ANA_INITIAL, ANA_VMIX, PACIFIC and
# LINEAR_DRAG_ONLY): &grid_settings ana_grid, &initial_conditions
# ana_initial and &vertical_mixing_settings ana_vmix (default .false.) are
# read, and .true. stops the run: the GPU has no analytical grid, initial
# state or vertical mixing. &v_sponge_settings sponge_profile = 'linear'
# (the default, as before) or 'cosine' (UCLA ROMS's former PACIFIC); another
# value stops. &bottom_drag_settings linear_drag = .true. (default .false.)
# uses the linear drag rdrg even when zob > 0.
#
# Periodic grids: the optional group &periodic_settings with the logicals
# ew_periodic, ns_periodic (default .false.; one direction may be periodic
# alone), as UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0; before, UCLA ROMS selected them with
# its cpp keys EW_PERIODIC and NS_PERIODIC. The size of the grid file no
# longer sets the periodicity: a grid file of LLm x MMm points (doubly
# periodic, the GPU's layout) now needs both keys, and stops the run without
# them. The grid file and the initial or restart file are each checked
# against the keys: a closed direction needs LLm+2 (MMm+2) rho points; a
# periodic one takes UCLA ROMS's layout, LLm+2 with the periodic copies as
# first and last points (only the interior is read), or roms_gpu's LLm
# (MMm). Any other size stops the run with the expected sizes. Output
# files keep roms_gpu's layout (no boundary points in a periodic
# direction), which UCLA ROMS cannot read.
#
# Open boundaries: the optional group &open_boundary_settings, as UCLA ROMS
# after 0.16.0; before, UCLA ROMS selected all of it with cpp keys (OBC_WEST,
# ...) and the GPU opened the sides it found zeta or barotropic velocity data
# for (with bry_tides and no boundary files, all four):
#   obc_west, obc_east, obc_south, obc_north   the open sides (default
#       .true.; ignored, with a start-up line, in a periodic direction). The
#       data of a closed side are ignored. A variable that is missing on an
#       open side (zeta, ubar, vbar, u, v, temp, salt) stops the run; before,
#       missing u, v, temp and salt were 0. So does a missing MARBL tracer
#       (before, 0 on inflow); CDR_LITE and generic passive tracers may be
#       absent and are then 0, as on UCLA ROMS. A namelist of a domain whose
#       boundary files hold only some sides must set the others to .false.
#   obc_m2, obc_m3, obc_t, obc_rad, use_m3_boundary_data,
#   use_t_boundary_data   the GPU has only the defaults ('flather',
#       'orlanski', 'orlanski', 'oblique', .true., .true.): with an open side,
#       any other value of UCLA ROMS stops the run.
#
# Surface restoring: logical keys in &surf_frc_settings (default .false.,
# bulk forcing only) switch it on, as in UCLA ROMS after 0.16.0; before,
# UCLA ROMS selected it with cpp keys. The coefficient group of a switch
# that is on must be present (the run stops otherwise; before, the GPU
# used 7.777 cm/day), as in UCLA ROMS:
#   old CPU cpp key    &surf_frc_settings             coefficient group (cm/day)
#   SFLX_CORR          sflx_corr = .true.             &sss_correction dSSSdt
#   QCORRECTION        qcorrection = .true.           &sst_correction dSSTdt
#   CFLX_CORR (MARBL)  cflx_corr = .true.             &dic_alk_correction dCdt
# A forcing file holding the restoring data (sss, sst, sDIC/sALK)
# while its switch is off gives a start-up warning. The restoring-flux
# output (&surf_flx_output_settings wrt_rstflx) is not on the GPU.
#
# Pressure fluxes for nesting: &calc_pflx_settings calc_pflx and
# pflx_timescale as UCLA ROMS (the group is optional here; absent means
# off). Both models compute up/vp whenever calc_pflx = .true. (UCLA ROMS
# up to 0.16.0 only when built with the DIAGNOSTICS cpp key); roms_gpu
# uses the internal-tide pressure of ucla-roms eae883ee, writes up_<side>/vp_<side>
# to the child boundary file for objects whose output_vars name them, and
# keeps u_slow, v_slow, p_slow in the restart. pflx_timescale must be > 0
# when calc_pflx is on (the run stops otherwise).
#
# Sponge tuning for nested children: &sponge_tune_settings apply_sponge_tune
# (default .false.; named ub_tune in UCLA ROMS up to 0.16.0, which also needs
# its SPONGE_TUNE cpp key; a namelist with ub_tune stops at the read) tunes the
# inflow nudging of the open boundaries to the parent's up/vp of the
# boundary files; it needs calc_pflx = .true. (the run stops otherwise), as
# UCLA ROMS. wrt_sponge writes <output_root_name>_spn.<date>.nc every
# output_period_sponge (nrpf_sponge records per file): the child and parent
# fluxes and the coefficient of every open side, averaged over the period
# (sponge_avg) or of the output step, as UCLA ROMS with its fixes of
# 2026-11 (sponge-tune-pio-fixes). sponge_avg defaults to .true., as in UCLA
# ROMS (before, .false.). As UCLA ROMS's precheck, with restarts, the
# tuning and wrt_sponge on, nrpf_sponge * output_period_sponge must be positive
# and divide output_period_rst (the run stops otherwise). The coefficients
# ub_west, ub_east, ub_south, ub_north are restart fields, written after
# the step's tuning (exact restarts), as in that version of UCLA ROMS.
#
# Implicit free surface (&implicit_fs, fs_mode = 'implicit'; absent or
# 'split': the split-explicit fast loop), as in ucla-roms
# implicit-fs-defaults. The settings (the five keys of UCLA ROMS's
# namelist template; defaults in brackets):
#   fs_mode     'split' | 'implicit'                                ['split']
#   fs_nsub     implicit sub-steps of dt/fs_nsub per step, 1..4     [2]
#   fs_rho_inf  spectral radius at infinite omega dt, in [0, 1)     [0.5]
#               (1, Crank-Nicolson, stops the run at the read)
#   fs_tol      relative residual of the elliptic solve             [1e-8]
#   fs_verbose  1: FS_SOLVE line per step; 2: + FS_VOL, FS_SRC,      [0]
#               FS_WALL lines (FS_SRC also with fs_mode = 'split')
# Solver and development settings: read as in UCLA ROMS, where the
# defaults are the recommended values, the keys may change between
# versions and C-Star and Forge do not expose them: fs_theta,
# fs_theta_div, fs_maxit (a solve that reaches it without meeting fs_tol
# stops the run), fs_precond, fs_mg_levels, fs_mg_nu, fs_mg_smoother,
# fs_mg_lag, fs_mg_faces, fs_drag_implicit, fs_warm, fs_tang_nudge,
# fs_cor_metric, fs_pot_time, fs_pg_rho, fs_flather_zghost (fs_rho_inf =
# 0, fs_nsub = 1, fs_pg_rho = fs_flather_zghost = .false. give the earlier
# single step); UCLA ROMS's MPI-layout keys fs_mg_gather, fs_mg_global_on
# and fs_exch_thin are read and not used; fs_selftest > 0 stops the run
# (the GPU has no solver self-test).
# GPU tuning settings (roms_gpu only): fs_gpu_gather, fs_gpu_coarse,
# fs_gpu_graph and fs_gpu_opt (layout and latency of the solve),
# fs_gpu_timers (timing runs: FS_COST, FS_WIN). fs_stress_time is no
# longer read (as in UCLA ROMS): a namelist that sets it stops at the
# read. Output files record fs_mode, and with 'implicit' fs_rho_inf and
# fs_nsub, as global attributes.
# Boundary options: roms_gpu's open edges have one barotropic type, UCLA
# ROMS's OBC_M2FLATHER (Flather normal faces, the zetabc sea level, the
# upwind tangential condition with inflow nudging), which the implicit
# free surface implements. The UCLA ROMS options for which the implicit
# step prints a start-up note there (OBC_M2ORLANSKI, open edges without an
# OBC_M2 type, OBC_Z2ORLANSKI, LEGACY_ORLANSKI, OBC_RAD_NORMAL, OBC_RAD_NPO)
# do not exist in roms_gpu, so it prints none.
# fs_gpu_opt is a bit mask in [0, 65535], default 65495 (was 471: bits
# 512 .. 32768 are new); bit 512 sums the PCG's partials of four ranks on
# one node in pairwise order instead of by MPI_Allreduce (GPU-only
# rounding-level difference), every other bit is bit-identical to 0. The
# solve stops the run on a NaN or Inf residual norm or <p,q>, with the
# CPU's message.
#
# Half-resolution forcing: interp_bulk_frc, interp_flux_frc
# (&surf_frc_settings) and interp_bgc_frc (&bgc_settings) are read but not
# used; roms_gpu takes a forcing field as half resolution from its shape
# ((LLm/2 + 2) x (MMm/2 + 2) at rho points, xi one shorter at u points,
# eta one shorter at v points) and interpolates it as UCLA ROMS does with
# the key on. A field that fits neither the model grid nor these shapes
# stops the run.
#
# Per-tracer lists: &vertical_mixing_settings akt_bak and &tracer_diff2 tnu2
# accept one value per tracer, as in UCLA ROMS (up to 512), in its tracer
# order (T, S, nt_passive generic, CDR_LITE, MARBL). Only akt_bak's T and S
# entries are used (as on the CPU, the other tracers mix with salinity's
# diffusivity). Values beyond the number of tracers are ignored, as in UCLA
# ROMS after 0.16.0. tnu2 is used per tracer, as UCLA ROMS: each
# tracer's harmonic diffusivity is its tnu2 plus the v_sponge_trc ramp. Generic
# passives added by the GPU-only &passive_tracers n_passive beyond nt_passive
# take salinity's tnu2.
#
# roms_gpu      UCLA ROMS namelist
